KPL/MYB

Tides of the Earth's gravity field after the IERS Conventions 2010 (IERS Technical Note 36,
chapter 6, version of 2018-02-01), read by myb_tides_create (myb/grav.h) with the prefix
'IERS10_TIDE'.

Sources:
  IERS Conventions 2010, chapter 6, https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/content/chapter6/icc6.pdf,
    SHA-256 abb3c0b0b6d2079b19893d6872a9d8e7320516d9a4736acb5eecaa79c4543388:
    Table 6.3 (Love numbers of the anelastic Earth), eq. 6.14 (permanent tide), Tables 6.5a,
    6.5b and 6.5c (frequency dependence of k21, k20, k22), section 6.4 (solid Earth pole tide),
    eq. 6.24 (ocean pole tide, degree 2);
  IERS Conventions 2010, chapter 7, https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/content/chapter7/icc7.pdf,
    SHA-256 ffe8ffb13c8bbc3b07ac298f458fcbb564974377b165fb93921a05bb0d55043d:
    eq. 21 (secular pole, used for the wobble m1 = xp - xs, m2 = -(yp - ys)).
  Downloaded on 2026-11-09. The 71 rows of Tables 6.5 were converted by a script that checks,
  for every row, the Doodson number against its six multipliers and those against the five
  Delaunay multipliers N (theta_f = m chi - N.F); amplitudes copied without change.

Step 1 (eq. 6.6, 6.7): dC_nm - i dS_nm = k_nm / (2n + 1) sum_j (GM_j / GM)(R / r_j)^(n+1)
  Pbar_nm(sin phi_j) exp(-i m lambda_j), n = 2, 3; degree 4 from the degree-2 tide with k_2m(+).
  LOVE: rows of (n, m, Re k_nm, Im k_nm, k_nm(+)).
Step 2 (eq. 6.8): series of dC20, dC21, dS21, dC22, dS22 over the arguments (chi, l, l', F, D,
  Omega), chi = GMST + pi, in the form of data/frames/iau2006-cip.tk (columns: power j,
  a_sin, a_cos, then the multipliers). For a row of Table 6.5 with amplitudes (ip, op):
    m = 0: dC20 = ip cos(theta) - op sin(theta)
    m = 1: dC21 = ip sin(theta) + op cos(theta),  dS21 = ip cos(theta) - op sin(theta)
    m = 2: dC22 = ip cos(theta),                  dS22 = -ip sin(theta)
  (the example of K1 in section 6.2.1: dC21 = 470.9e-12 sin(chi) - 30.2e-12 cos(chi)).
  The argument t is in Julian centuries of 36525 days from J2000.0 of UT1 (chi is GMST); the
  arguments are those of data/frames/eop-tides.tk.
Step 3 (eq. 6.13, 6.14): for a zero-tide field the permanent part A0 H0 Re(k20) is removed
  from dC20. PERMANENT = ( A0 H0 ) in m^-1 and m.
Pole tide (sections 6.4, 6.5): dC21 = c1 (m1 + a1 m2), dS21 = c2 (m2 + a2 m1) with m1, m2 in
  arcseconds; POLE_SOLID and POLE_OCEAN = ( c1 a1 c2 a2 ). SECULAR_POLE = ( xs0 xs1 ys0 ys1 )
  in milliarcseconds: xs = xs0 + xs1 (t - 2000), t in Julian years.

\begindata

